Distributed Tetris over a LAN

Python

Main libraries:
-PyGame
-socket
-threading

Major Problems:
- How to represent blocks and thier rotations
- LAN connection
- LAN communication
- Shifting tetris: blocks collision when shifting

Grid:
Grid is just a 10x20 2D array with each cell in one grid tile and its value is representing color of placed block on a grid where 0 is empty tile

LAN Module
  The whole LAN module is implemented in lan_connection.py file as a class Peer
  The class has methods:
  - get_my_ip(self):
    . returns host ip in current local network
  - get_broadcast_ip(self):
   . returns broadcast ip in local network
  - change_ready_status(self):
   . changes ready status in lobby and also sends message to all other players about current ready status
  - search_for_peers(self):
    . while this method is not stopped, it is searching for players in local network by broadcasting discovery msg for one of gamemodes
      only players searching the same gamemode are recognised and then added to player list which contains also player ready status
  - broadcast(self):
    . while this method is not stopped, it is broadcasting discovery msg
  - send_msg_to_all_players(self, msg):
    . sends msg to every player in the game
  - send_msg_to_one_player(self, player_ip, msg):
    . sends msg to one specific player in the game
  - listen(self):
    . it listnes for new messages from players while game is running, when there is any then it puts ti in recived msg deque
  - quit(self):
    . sends to every player information about player disconnecting
    
